From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:08:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] fix: use PhysicalStorageBuffer storage for BDA access
 chains

Problem: atomics on a vector component reached through a buffer_reference
(BDA) pointer emitted "&vec[0]", which is invalid MSL.

Root cause: the BDA pointer is usually loaded from a push constant or UBO,
so get_expression_effective_storage_class returned that block's storage
class instead of PhysicalStorageBuffer, and the MSL scalar-access path
did not handle PhysicalStorageBuffer.

Fix: in the vector-to-scalar access-chain path, treat a base whose type
is a PhysicalStorageBuffer pointer as PhysicalStorageBuffer, and accept
PhysicalStorageBuffer in prepare_access_chain_for_scalar_access.

Verified by: see NOTES.md Finding 3.

Off switch: none.
---
 spirv_glsl.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 spirv_msl.cpp  | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/spirv_glsl.cpp b/spirv_glsl.cpp
index 79db239..1e27d30 100644
--- a/spirv_glsl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_glsl.cpp
@@ -11458,7 +11458,14 @@ string CompilerGLSL::access_chain_internal(uint32_t base, const uint32_t *indice
 			if ((flags & ACCESS_CHAIN_FORCE_COMPOSITE_BIT) == 0)
 			{
 				if (expression_type(base).pointer)
-					effective_storage = get_expression_effective_storage_class(base);
+				{
+					// A buffer_reference (BDA) pointer is often loaded from a push constant or UBO, so the
+					// backing variable is that block. The memory accessed through it is PhysicalStorageBuffer.
+					if (expression_type(base).storage == StorageClassPhysicalStorageBuffer)
+						effective_storage = StorageClassPhysicalStorageBuffer;
+					else
+						effective_storage = get_expression_effective_storage_class(base);
+				}
 
 				// Special consideration for control points.
 				// Control points can only be written by InvocationID, so there is no need
diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
index f421f15..0f679dc 100644
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -9788,7 +9788,8 @@ bool CompilerMSL::prepare_access_chain_for_scalar_access(std::string &expr, cons
 	// For packed types, we could technically omit this if we know the reference does not have to turn into a pointer
 	// of some kind, but that requires external analysis passes to figure out, and
 	// this case is likely rare enough that we don't need to bother.
-	if (storage == StorageClassStorageBuffer || storage == StorageClassWorkgroup)
+	if (storage == StorageClassStorageBuffer || storage == StorageClassPhysicalStorageBuffer ||
+	    storage == StorageClassWorkgroup)
 	{
 		const char *addr_space = storage == StorageClassWorkgroup ? "threadgroup" : "device";
 		expr = join("((", addr_space, " ", type_to_glsl(type), "*)&", enclose_expression(expr), ")");
